---
const titleId = 'diagram-compression-pause-title';
const descId = 'diagram-compression-pause-desc';
---

<figure class="diagram" data-diagram="compression-pause">
  <svg
    viewBox="0 0 320 400"
    role="img"
    aria-labelledby={titleId}
    aria-describedby={descId}
  >
    <title id={titleId}>Schematic, not measured data. When compressions continue, coronary perfusion pressure builds. When they pause, it falls. When compressions resume, it builds again along a continuous rise.</title>
    <desc id={descId}>A timeline of continuous curves, not a measured curve and not a numbered scale. The line rises while compressions continue. At the pause, an arrow shows perfusion pressure falling to the baseline. After the pause, a smooth unlabeled ramp rises again, with no compression count and no duration. No axis values are shown.</desc>

    <rect class="diagram-banner" x="0" y="0" width="320" height="48"></rect>
    <rect class="diagram-mark" x="0" y="0" width="4" height="48"></rect>
    <text class="diagram-schematic" x="16" y="30" font-size="15">Schematic, not measured data</text>

    <text class="diagram-kicker" x="16" y="78" font-size="14">Timeline</text>
    <text class="diagram-display" x="16" y="108" font-size="18">Perfusion pressure</text>
    <text class="diagram-note" x="16" y="136" font-size="15">Continuous rise, not a counted run.</text>

    <line class="diagram-baseline" x1="16" y1="268" x2="304" y2="268"></line>

    <path class="diagram-ramp" d="M16 268 C48 268 64 156 100 156 L124 156 L124 268 Z"></path>
    <path class="diagram-ramp-line" d="M16 268 C48 268 64 156 100 156 L124 156"></path>

    <line class="diagram-fall" x1="124" y1="156" x2="140" y2="156"></line>
    <line class="diagram-fall" x1="140" y1="156" x2="140" y2="254"></line>
    <polygon class="diagram-fall-head" points="140,268 133,254 147,254"></polygon>

    <path class="diagram-ramp" d="M196 268 C230 266 250 230 304 180 L304 268 Z"></path>
    <path class="diagram-ramp-line" d="M196 268 C230 266 250 230 304 180"></path>

    <text class="diagram-label" x="70" y="300" font-size="15" text-anchor="middle">Builds</text>
    <text class="diagram-label" x="168" y="300" font-size="15" text-anchor="middle">Pause</text>
    <text class="diagram-label" x="168" y="322" font-size="15" text-anchor="middle">falls</text>
    <text class="diagram-label" x="250" y="300" font-size="15" text-anchor="middle">Rebuilds</text>

    <text class="diagram-label" x="16" y="366" font-size="15">Time</text>
    <line class="diagram-time" x1="58" y1="361" x2="286" y2="361"></line>
    <polygon class="diagram-time-head" points="304,361 292,355 292,367"></polygon>
  </svg>
  <figcaption>
    <p class="kicker">Figure</p>
    <p>
      Schematic, not measured data. When compressions continue, coronary perfusion pressure builds.
      When they pause, it falls. When compressions resume, it builds again. The rise is continuous
      and does not mark a set number of compressions or a duration. There is no scale and no measured
      curve.
    </p>
  </figcaption>
</figure>
